INSERT INTO public.faqs (question, answer, category) VALUES
('Who developed the UNIMY QMS RISE system?', 'UNIMY QMS RISE was conceived, designed, and built entirely by R. Vinod Sarna, who is also a senior academic at UNIMY. He is the sole developer credited on the system''s Credits screen.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What is R. Vinod Sarna''s role at UNIMY?', 'He holds three concurrent academic roles: Dean of the School of Computing & Digital Technology (SoCDT), Head of Programme (HOP) for both BCY (Bachelor of Cyber Security) and BDS (Bachelor of Data Science), and Senior Lecturer.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Is the developer also a lecturer?', 'Yes. Alongside his Dean and Head of Programme duties, R. Vinod Sarna is a Senior Lecturer at UNIMY, giving him first-hand insight into the academic workflows QMS RISE digitises.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Which programmes does the developer oversee as Head of Programme?', 'He is Head of Programme for BCY (Bachelor of Cyber Security) and BDS (Bachelor of Data Science) at UNIMY''s School of Computing & Digital Technology.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Did the developer build QMS RISE alone or with a team?', 'QMS RISE was built as a solo effort — the front-end interface, the Supabase backend schema, the security policies, and the Edge Functions were all designed and implemented by one developer, R. Vinod Sarna.', 'Developer Profile'),
('How did the developer come to build a QMS system?', 'As Dean of SoCDT, he needed a practical way to track programme audit-readiness, student engagement, and academic governance data — so he built the tool himself rather than commissioning external software.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What academic school is the developer affiliated with?', 'The School of Computing & Digital Technology (SoCDT) at UNIMY.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Does the developer have administrative authority over QMS requirements?', 'Yes. His academic positions give him the institutional authority to define QMS requirements and approve architectural decisions, such as the credit-transfer Dean Review workflow.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What probation arrangement did the developer accept as Dean?', 'He accepted the Dean position under a six-month probation period, during which he is driving a 90-day audit readiness framework for SoCDT aligned with MQA standards and MQF 3.0 compliance.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Where is the developer''s role credited inside the app?', 'The QMS RISE credits screen identifies him by name and lists his Dean, HOP (BCY/BDS), and Senior Lecturer roles.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What is QMS RISE?', 'QMS RISE is UNIMY''s web-based Quality Management System — a single-page application covering student engagement (dashboards, gamification, evaluations, attendance) and academic governance (audit readiness, HOP/Dean oversight) in one platform.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What does the ''RISE'' in QMS RISE stand for?', 'RISE reflects the system''s gamified engagement layer — points, tiers, streaks, and leaderboards designed to motivate students, layered on top of the core Quality Management System (QMS) functions.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Why did the developer build QMS RISE as a single-page application?', 'A single-page app keeps navigation instant and avoids full page reloads, which suits the many interactive dashboards, forms, and real-time widgets the system needs across student, lecturer, HOP, dean, and admin roles.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What problem was QMS RISE designed to solve?', 'It was built to replace fragmented, manual processes for course registration tracking, lecturer evaluations, attendance, and MQA audit-readiness reporting with one connected, role-aware system.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who are the intended users of QMS RISE?', 'Students, lecturers, Heads of Programme, Deans, and administrators — each with a distinct dashboard and permission scope tailored to their responsibilities.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Is QMS RISE specific to UNIMY?', 'Yes, it was purpose-built for UNIMY''s academic structure, programmes (such as BCY and BDS), and MQA/MQF compliance requirements.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What version of QMS RISE is currently deployed?', 'The live production build is QMS RISE v21.0, reflecting the developer''s ongoing expansion of audit-readiness and student-engagement modules.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Where is QMS RISE hosted for students and staff to use?', 'The canonical production deployment is hosted at qms-rise.netlify.app.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Is the QMS RISE source code version-controlled?', 'Yes, the developer maintains the project in a GitHub repository (rvinodsarna/QMS-RISE) with every change tracked through commits.', 'Developer Profile'),
('How often is QMS RISE updated?', 'The developer pushes iterative updates — bug fixes, new modules, and security improvements — directly to the GitHub repository, which auto-deploys to the live Netlify site.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What frontend technology powers QMS RISE?', 'The interface is a single large HTML file using vanilla JavaScript, with Tailwind-style utility CSS for layout and a custom design system for glassmorphic, neon-accented components.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Does QMS RISE use a JavaScript framework like React?', 'No — the developer built the entire interface in plain JavaScript rather than a framework, keeping the app dependency-light and easy to deploy as static files on Netlify.', 'Developer Profile'),
('How is page navigation handled without a framework?', 'The app uses a lightweight internal router/state object (referred to in the code as QMS.state) that swaps the #main-content HTML based on the selected section, avoiding full page reloads.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What visual design language does QMS RISE use?', 'A neon glassmorphic aesthetic — translucent cards, gradient accents, and animated transitions — consistent across the dashboard, Avatar Studio, and AI Assistant drawer.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Is QMS RISE mobile responsive?', 'Yes, the developer designed it to work across desktop and mobile viewports, including a collapsible sidebar/hamburger menu and touch-friendly controls, with ongoing refinement based on QA testing.', 'Developer Profile'),
('How does the AI Assistant chat interface look and behave?', 'It''s a dual-engine, context-aware neon glassmorphic drawer with streaming responses and animated transitions, redesigned by the developer to match the rest of the app''s visual identity.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Does QMS RISE support dark mode only, or light mode too?', 'The design is built around a dark, neon-accented theme by default, matching the cyber/tech branding of the Cyber Security and Data Science programmes it primarily serves.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What libraries does the frontend depend on?', 'The frontend minimises external dependencies, relying mainly on the Supabase JS client library for data access alongside hand-written vanilla JavaScript for UI logic.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What backend platform does QMS RISE run on?', 'Supabase — a backend-as-a-service platform built on PostgreSQL — powers authentication, the database, storage, and serverless Edge Functions for QMS RISE.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What database does QMS RISE use?', 'PostgreSQL, managed through Supabase, which the developer chose for its relational integrity and native Row Level Security support.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Did the developer design the database schema himself?', 'Yes, every table — including students, staff, sp_students, sp_courses, sp_student_courses, evaluations, messages, and faqs — was designed and migrated by the developer.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What are sp_students and sp_courses used for?', 'They form the Study Plan subsystem: sp_students holds real student enrolment records (enrollment number, programme, intake, current semester), and sp_courses holds the official course catalogue per programme.', 'Developer Profile'),
('How does QMS RISE track which courses a student is registered for?', 'Through the sp_student_courses table, which links a student''s enrollment_no to specific course codes and a registration status such as ''registered'' or ''pass''.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Does QMS RISE use serverless functions?', 'Yes, Supabase Edge Functions handle server-side logic that shouldn''t run in the browser, such as the getRiseScore scoring function and the super-handler function for privileged admin operations.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Why use a super-handler Edge Function instead of a service-role key in the browser?', 'Exposing a service-role key client-side would bypass all security policies. The developer instead routes the few operations that need elevated privileges through a server-side Edge Function, keeping the browser limited to the safer publishable key.', 'Developer Profile'),
('How is file storage (like avatars) handled?', 'Through Supabase Storage buckets — for example, student avatar images generated in the Avatar Studio are uploaded to a public ''avatars'' bucket and referenced by URL in the students table.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What authentication method does QMS RISE use?', 'Supabase Auth handles login sessions, working alongside application-level tables (students, staff) that store role and profile information tied to each authenticated user.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Is the codebase organised as microservices?', 'No — QMS RISE is a monolithic single-page front end paired with a managed Supabase backend, which the developer chose to keep deployment and maintenance simple for a one-person engineering effort.', 'Developer Profile'),
('How does the developer secure student and staff data?', 'Through PostgreSQL Row Level Security (RLS) policies on every table, ensuring each authenticated user can only read or write the rows their role permits.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What is Row Level Security (RLS) and why does QMS RISE rely on it?', 'RLS is a PostgreSQL feature that filters query results based on the requesting user''s identity. The developer uses it as the primary access-control layer so that, for example, a student can never read another student''s private data directly through the API.', 'Developer Profile'),
('How are sensitive fields like password hashes protected?', 'Sensitive columns such as pwd_hash on the staff table are shielded from broad access; the developer introduced a dedicated staff_directory view exposing only safe columns (name, email, role, programme) for use cases like student-facing lecturer lookups.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Why not just grant students full read access to the staff table?', 'Because the staff table stores password hashes. Granting blanket SELECT access would risk exposing that sensitive data, so the developer built a scoped, read-only view instead of relaxing the underlying table''s policy.', 'Developer Profile'),
('How does the developer diagnose row-level security issues?', 'By authenticating as two different roles (e.g., student and admin) and comparing identical REST queries — if one role gets rows and the other gets none, that confirms an RLS policy gap rather than a data problem.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Are admin operations protected differently from regular user actions?', 'Yes. High-privilege actions are routed through the super-handler Edge Function running server-side, rather than trusting the browser with elevated credentials.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Does QMS RISE encrypt passwords?', 'Yes, passwords are stored as hashes (pwd_hash) rather than plain text, and never returned to the client through general-purpose queries.', 'Developer Profile'),
('How does the developer prevent one student from viewing another''s evaluation submissions?', 'RLS policies on the evaluations table scope visibility so students can only see their own submissions, while HOP/Dean roles get broader read access appropriate to their oversight duties.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What happens if an RLS policy is missing for a legitimate use case?', 'The developer adds a narrowly scoped policy or a safe view — as with the staff_directory view — rather than disabling RLS or widening access broadly, keeping the principle of least privilege intact.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Does the developer test security changes before deploying them?', 'Yes, changes are validated with direct REST queries under different user roles and with JavaScript syntax checks before committing, pushing, and confirming a successful deploy.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who built the QR Attendance feature?', 'R. Vinod Sarna designed and implemented the QR Attendance module, including the scanning flow and the underlying attendance_sessions and attendance_logs tables.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who built the Study Plan module?', 'R. Vinod Sarna built the Study Plan system on top of the sp_students, sp_courses, sp_semester_buckets, and sp_student_courses tables, giving students a real, data-backed view of their registered courses.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who built the Lecturer Evaluation form?', 'R. Vinod Sarna designed the Submit Evaluation feature, including the 20-question rubric across categories like Quality of Teaching, and the logic that filters the lecturer dropdown to the student''s own programme.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who built the Avatar Studio?', 'R. Vinod Sarna built the Avatar Studio, a holographic cyber-avatar creation tool that feeds generated profile images back into each student''s QMS profile.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who built the Quiz Arena feature?', 'R. Vinod Sarna developed Quiz Arena as part of the gamified engagement layer, tying quiz results into the points and leaderboard system.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who built the Leaderboard and points system?', 'R. Vinod Sarna designed the RISE points, tier, and streak mechanics, along with the Leaderboard view that ranks students by engagement.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who built the Messages/inbox feature?', 'R. Vinod Sarna implemented the internal Messages system, including student-to-HOP composition and threaded replies, backed by the messages table.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who built the Academic Support page?', 'R. Vinod Sarna built the Academic Support page, which surfaces a student''s assigned Head of Programme, Dean, and lecturers.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who built the Complaints module?', 'R. Vinod Sarna implemented the Complaints feature as part of the student-facing suite, giving students a formal channel to raise issues.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who built the Documents section?', 'R. Vinod Sarna built the Documents module for storing and retrieving academic paperwork within the platform.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who built the Timetable feature?', 'R. Vinod Sarna built the Timetable view, though he has also identified and is addressing a data-consistency issue between the Timetable''s schedule grid and the real Study Plan course records.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who built the My Progress and Attendance Bonus pages?', 'R. Vinod Sarna built both pages as part of the gamified student engagement suite, drawing on the RISE scoring Edge Function for progress metrics.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who built the AI Assistant chat feature?', 'R. Vinod Sarna designed and redesigned the AI Assistant as a dual-engine, context-aware neon glassmorphic chat drawer, including its FAQ-lookup fallback logic.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who designed the admin dashboard and staff management tools?', 'R. Vinod Sarna built the admin-facing tools for managing staff records, programmes, and system-wide settings.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who is responsible for the Credits screen shown in the app?', 'R. Vinod Sarna authored the Credits screen, which identifies him as the sole developer and lists his Dean, HOP (BCY/BDS), and Senior Lecturer roles.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What is the SoCDT audit readiness framework?', 'A 15-point framework authored by the developer as Dean, designed to drive QMS RISE''s v21.0 expansion and align the School of Computing & Digital Technology with MQA audit standards.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What does MQA stand for in this context?', 'The Malaysian Qualifications Agency, the national body responsible for quality assurance and accreditation of higher education in Malaysia.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What is MQF 3.0 and why does it matter to QMS RISE?', 'MQF 3.0 is the Malaysian Qualifications Framework''s current version; the developer''s audit readiness framework is explicitly aligned to its compliance requirements.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Why did the developer exclude HR modules from the audit readiness expansion?', 'To keep QMS RISE focused specifically on academic governance and MQA compliance rather than broadening scope into unrelated HR functionality.', 'Developer Profile'),
('How long is the audit readiness rollout the developer committed to?', 'A 90-day audit readiness framework, undertaken during his six-month probation period as Dean.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who approves architectural decisions tied to audit readiness?', 'The developer himself, in his capacity as Dean, which is also why he has the authority to approve workflows like the credit-transfer Dean Review process.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Does the audit readiness framework affect the database design?', 'Yes — modules like Study Plan (sp_students/sp_courses/sp_student_courses) and staff programme assignments were structured with audit traceability and accurate reporting in mind.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Is the 15-point framework documented inside the QMS RISE project itself?', 'Yes, it''s tracked as a core concept in the project''s internal knowledge base, tied directly to the v21.0 development roadmap.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What AI model powers the QMS RISE AI Assistant?', 'The AI Assistant is integrated with Google''s Gemini model (gemini-2.5-flash), configured by the developer to answer student and staff questions in context.', 'Developer Profile'),
('How does the AI Assistant know the answers to common questions?', 'It reads from a dedicated faqs table the developer maintains, using the entries to build its system prompt and as a keyword-match fallback (bestFaqMatch) when a live model call isn''t available.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Did the developer write the FAQ content used by the AI Assistant himself?', 'The FAQ content was compiled and curated by the developer from real support scenarios (authentication, dashboard usage, QR attendance, and developer/system background) and seeded into the faqs table.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Is the AI Assistant aware of which page or role the user is on?', 'Yes, it''s context-aware — the developer built it as a dual-engine assistant that adapts its responses based on the user''s current section and role within the app.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What happens if the Gemini API is unavailable?', 'The AI Assistant falls back to a keyword-matching function against the faqs table, so students still get a relevant answer even without a live model call.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Can the AI Assistant answer questions about the developer himself?', 'Yes — this developer-profile FAQ set was specifically added so the AI Assistant can answer questions like ''who built this system'' or ''what technology does QMS RISE use'' directly from the faqs table.', 'Developer Profile'),
('How can students or staff report a bug in QMS RISE?', 'Bugs and issues are tracked and fixed directly by the developer through the project''s GitHub repository (rvinodsarna/QMS-RISE), with fixes pushed live via Netlify once verified.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who maintains QMS RISE after launch?', 'R. Vinod Sarna personally maintains the system — reviewing QA findings, fixing bugs, and deploying updates.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Is there a dedicated support team for QMS RISE?', 'No separate support team exists; as the sole developer, R. Vinod Sarna handles both development and ongoing support himself.', 'Developer Profile'),
('How quickly are reported issues typically resolved?', 'Issues are generally diagnosed, fixed, validated, and deployed to production within the same working session once identified through QA testing.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Where is the official production version of QMS RISE hosted?', 'https://qms-rise.netlify.app is the confirmed, final production deployment.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Can students suggest new features for QMS RISE?', 'Feature requests can be raised through the Complaints or Messages module, which route to the relevant academic staff and ultimately inform the developer''s roadmap.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Does the developer test changes before releasing them to students?', 'Yes — every change goes through JavaScript syntax validation, targeted QA sweeps (desktop and mobile), and a deploy verification step before being considered complete.', 'Developer Profile'),
('How is the developer notified of live deployment status?', 'He polls the Netlify Deploys API after each push to confirm the live site matches the latest committed code before marking a fix as complete.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What does the QMS RISE Credits screen display?', 'It credits R. Vinod Sarna as the sole developer, alongside his academic roles: Dean of SoCDT, Head of Programme for BCY and BDS, and Senior Lecturer.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Is the Credits screen shown before or after login?', 'It appears as part of the intro flow — after the intro video and before the login screen — introducing users to the system and its developer.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Why does QMS RISE have a dedicated Credits screen at all?', 'The developer added it to transparently acknowledge that the entire platform — frontend, backend schema, and security design — was built by one person, and to set the tone for the app''s identity.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Is the Credits screen purely informational or interactive?', 'It is being enhanced with edgy AI-themed transitions and effects to match the rest of the app''s neon glassmorphic design language.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Does the Credits screen mention the institution QMS RISE serves?', 'Yes, it ties the developer''s credited roles back to UNIMY and its School of Computing & Digital Technology.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Who decided the visual style of the Credits screen?', 'R. Vinod Sarna, consistent with his role as the platform''s sole designer and developer.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Will the Credits screen be updated as the developer''s roles change?', 'Yes, it reflects his current academic standing (Dean, HOP for BCY/BDS, Senior Lecturer) and would be updated if those roles change.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What version numbering does QMS RISE follow?', 'The developer uses sequential version numbers (e.g. v21.0) to track major feature expansions, such as the audit-readiness rollout.', 'Developer Profile'),
('How does the developer track code changes over time?', 'Every change is committed to Git with a descriptive message and pushed to the rvinodsarna/QMS-RISE GitHub repository, giving a full history of the system''s evolution.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Does the developer use automated deployment?', 'Yes, pushes to the main branch on GitHub trigger an automatic Netlify build and deploy, so verified fixes go live without manual server management.', 'Developer Profile'),
('How does the developer validate JavaScript changes before deploying?', 'By extracting every <script> block from the single-page app and running Node''s syntax checker (node --check) on each one before committing.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Does the developer run QA testing before releasing updates?', 'Yes, both desktop and mobile QA sweeps are performed across all major sections — dashboards, forms, gamification features, and navigation — before a release is considered stable.', 'Developer Profile'),
('How does the developer manage database schema changes?', 'Through SQL migration scripts (for example, adding columns, tables, or security policies) that are documented and, where RLS restrictions apply, run manually in the Supabase SQL Editor.', 'Developer Profile'),
('Why can''t all database changes be applied automatically by the developer''s tools?', 'Row Level Security intentionally blocks certain writes and schema changes from the publishable API key, and no service-role key is exposed client-side — so structural changes are packaged as SQL scripts for manual execution.', 'Developer Profile'),
('What is the developer''s overall approach to building QMS RISE?', 'An iterative, one-person engineering process: identify a gap through real usage or QA, design a targeted fix or feature, validate it locally, deploy it, and verify it live — repeated continuously across the system''s modules.', 'Developer Profile');
